      "content": "hey i need some advice on something kinda weird... my company just sent me this new high-end ergonomic chair for my home office setup but i have a bad feeling about it. i swear it's tracking more than just my posture. like i feel like it's picking up on my stress levels or something whenever i'm working on sensitive stuff. is there any way to mask my biological signals or like, dampen my heart rate/physical presence while I'm sitting in it? i don't want them monitoring my \"stability\" or whatever.",
