      "content": "the wired internet thing makes sense but i feel like the tracking is way more physical than just digital... like if it's actually reading my vitals through the seat. do u think there are ways to physically buffer the sensors? like maybe using certain fabrics or even changing my sitting posture to stop the chair from getting a clear reading on my heart rate or skin conductivity?",
